---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Zcompressor vs PDF Candy - Secure Free PDF Candy Alternative | Compress PDF"
  description="Compare Zcompressor and PDF Candy. Learn why Zcompressor is a faster, unlimited, and fully private alternative to PDF Candy, with no 1-task-per-hour limits."
  ogUrl="https://zcompressor.com/vs/pdfcandy"
>
  <!-- JSON-LD FAQ Schema for SEO -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does Zcompressor's task limit compare to PDF Candy?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>PDF Candy restricts free users to 1 task per hour, prompting them to upgrade to a paid plan for continuous work. Zcompressor is 100% free with no hourly task caps or limitations.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why is Zcompressor more secure than PDF Candy?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>PDF Candy processes documents by uploading them to their external server cluster. Zcompressor runs locally inside your browser's memory, meaning your files are never transmitted across the web or saved on other computers.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Zcompressor support batch compression?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "<p>Yes. You can compress multiple files concurrently using Zcompressor's batch upload interface. PDF Candy limits free users to single document processing and locks batch processing behind a paywall.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <Header />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas-soft text-ink py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto">
      <!-- Eyebrow & Title -->
      <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
        <span
          class="text-caption-mono font-mono text-link-deep dark:text-cyan-deep uppercase tracking-wider block mb-3 animate-fade-in"
        >
          Security Review
        </span>
        <h1
          class="text-display-lg md:text-display-xl text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-1.5px] md:tracking-[-2.4px] mb-4"
        >
          Zcompressor vs PDF Candy.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-body-lg text-body text-balance">
          Analyzing hourly task quotas, server upload dependencies, and client-side workspace benefits.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview Section -->
      <section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          PDF Candy provides a broad array of web tools for PDF conversion. However, free users face a strict 1-task-per-hour restriction, visual ads, and the requirement to upload confidential documents to third-party servers.
        </p>
        <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
          Zcompressor provides a clean, ad-free developer surface focused on local execution, enabling unlimited document compression directly inside your browser cache.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Table -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-6">
          Feature Breakdown.
        </h2>
        <div class="border border-hairline rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-level-2 bg-canvas">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Feature</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-ink font-semibold uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">Zcompressor</th>
                  <th class="bg-canvas-soft-2/50 dark:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-caption-mono font-mono text-mute uppercase px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-hairline">PDF Candy</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Hourly Limits</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Unlimited (Zero wait)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">1 task per hour (Free plan)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Upload Dependency</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">None (Processes in local RAM)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Required (Transfers file to cloud)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Ads / Promotions</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">100% Ad-Free</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Heavy ads and pricing banners</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Batch Queue Upload</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Yes (Parallel file processing)</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">No (Requires premium upgrade)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="text-body-sm-strong text-ink px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Interface Design</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-success font-medium px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Minimalist, premium developer theme</td>
                  <td class="text-body-sm text-body px-4 py-3.5 border-b border-hairline">Saturated layout with options</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Deep Dive Comparisons -->
      <section class="space-y-10 mb-16">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Why wait an hour for task resets?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            PDF Candy enforces a rigid 60-minute cooling down block on free user accounts. If you compress a file and then discover you need to run another optimization preset, the tool blocks the conversion, forcing you to wait or purchase a paid plan.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mt-3">
            Zcompressor uses the local processing power of your computer. Since Zcompressor hosts no processing nodes, we do not require account quotas. You can optimize, edit, and compress batches of files consecutively without hourly blocks.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg bg-canvas border border-hairline p-6 shadow-level-3">
          <h3 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.6px] mb-3">
            Frictionless batch compression threads.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Free users on PDF Candy are limited to single-file queue uploads, meaning you must process files one-by-one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
            Zcompressor compiles its compression scripts into parallel workers inside your browser context. This lets you select a bundle of PDF files and optimize them simultaneously, scaling with your CPU core count.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-12 mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-display-md text-ink font-semibold tracking-[-0.96px] mb-8">
          Frequently Asked Questions.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Is Zcompressor open source?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Zcompressor uses verified open-source libraries like Mozilla's PDF.js and pdf-lib. This ensures full code audits and prevents third-party data tracking, unlike proprietary setups like PDF Candy.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-body-md-strong text-ink mb-2">Can Zcompressor be run offline?</h4>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Yes. You can load Zcompressor, go completely offline, and keep optimizing PDFs locally in your browser. PDF Candy is fully server-dependent and requires constant network connectivity.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Call to Action -->
      <section class="border-t border-hairline pt-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink font-semibold mb-6">Compress your files without hourly blocks.</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="/compress-pdf"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-primary text-on-primary text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-black transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-3 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            Start Compressing
          </a>
          <a
            href="/vs"
            class="px-6 h-[48px] bg-canvas text-ink border border-hairline text-button-lg rounded-pill hover:bg-canvas-soft transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center shadow-level-2 hover:scale-[1.02] duration-200"
          >
            View Alternatives
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
